  SC_n5_#3 (n=5): H(T)=1 (ODD), rho:HP->HP=True, involution=True, #palindromic=1 (ODD), H==#palin mod2: True
      example palindromic path: (4, 3, 0, 2, 1)  (rho = (4, 3, 0, 2, 1))
   n=5: 704 self-converse tournaments (with involutory phi) found

================================================================================
Conclusion: for self-converse T with involutory anti-aut phi, rho=phi.reverse
is an involution on Ham paths => H(T) == #palindromic (mod2); Redei (H odd)
=> ODD number of palindromic Ham paths >=1.  This is the sigma-ODD index
(witness side); the LRC lonely measure is the sigma-EVEN index (existence).
================================================================================
